      "canonicalConceptId": "concept:008ab3361c0ee24999b82766299cf49f626db9368854073f8e444a7fb1917f94",
      "text": "A crypto bot monitor must distinguish provisional inclusion from chain-specific finality and detect when previously observed chain evidence changes. Solana commitment and blockhash expiry, Ethereum checkpoint finality, and OP Stack settlement stages need different treatment. Hash continuity, rollback-aware ingestion and consistent event/header evidence support reorg detection. Historical finality incidents and client issues show why transaction availability and notification assumptions need separate checks. Indexer rollback does not automatically undo external actions. These findings support explicit commitment tracking and reconciliation rather than a universal confirmation count.",
